  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_cba40c5ca8d347e2bb1fc79a625b607d",
      "statement": "BidPoint requires each artifact and setting to have exactly one semantic owner: backend application behavior belongs to `config/`, Kubernetes workload operation belongs to `gitops/`, cloud foundations belong to `infra/`, and each frontend owns its own non-sensitive settings.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://AGENTS.md#L32-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ec821abb9848bba0ca0cc578648fd972ee62021f5d62ec73245cfc418afb8a0b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/README.md#L31-L33",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7594975e42904a0d5761f79d1ea37a5acaf0095ab5c2cc0005a7987755937e0c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_80bde0bf1c7f4edc9b702dc1797aaa69",
      "statement": "`config/` is the source of truth for non-sensitive backend behavior settings, including service and messaging endpoints, feature flags, timeouts, retries, behavior switches, logging, and eventual per-environment variants; it does not own Kubernetes state, infrastructure, frontend configuration, code, or plaintext secrets.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://config/README.md#L13-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:463f90abb3b24de8087bf97dd75bafc8362b8e6112d7e055d01c6d12b8b91b23:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a4a42408cb7f4afb90185ad2431fee16",
      "statement": "`gitops/` owns desired Kubernetes workload state for an already-existing cluster, including image versions, replicas, resources, Services, identities, ingress, probes, autoscaling, deployment strategies, platform workloads, and per-environment sizing; it does not provision cloud resources or own backend behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://gitops/README.md#L1-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ee124952352ee13eb297f0534688043a63e8e8c498148d6a3608a685939da62f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_15abed155f574e0c94f4dd9167c87237",
      "statement": "The primary `config/` versus `gitops/` placement test is which process interprets the value: Kubernetes consumes GitOps declarations at pod creation, whereas the backend consumes application settings at startup and on refresh; generic workload controls or values that survive deleting backend code belong to `gitops/`, while BidPoint-specific behavior belongs to `config/`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://config/README.md#L31-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:52333bf147185f812527b606453d734c21862dcaf3748121f0feba2460e064f2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://gitops/README.md#L28-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9d599f2b220a311b66aba43989a90d0ef8a2dc461a652dd8ab23e6afad3ceb5d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8048d6920d444034874fb21b4da0fe2c",
      "statement": "A backend workload in `gitops/` may set only `SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE`, `SPRING_APPLICATION_NAME`, and `SPRING_CONFIG_IMPORT`, plus secret-backed variables sourced from Kubernetes Secrets; the three named variables provide the bootstrap identity and location needed to fetch application configuration.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://config/README.md#L46-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:817b41248af3ef6976f531845c32429ebed10deef300d596224f640917b664ad:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://gitops/README.md#L32-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a4a83910972ccbcff11761d4bc8a4315cc16f89141a34ee3a9bd2886cbb2a6bc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_550eb31b82184e18a936f067d066199f",
      "statement": "Declaring any other backend behavior variable in `gitops/` duplicates `config/` ownership and can fail silently because Spring Boot relaxed binding treats forms such as `BID_TIMEOUT` and `bid.timeout` as the same property while an environment variable can outrank the configuration-server value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://config/README.md#L57-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc136ae8b442909ae8ae34c119f1a4e2ac66b0aa3963eefba4f0b0fa6b35556b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1d2216231be64da082a25ce1d2faa6f4",
      "statement": "Backend behavior is expected to be delivered from `config/` through Spring Cloud Config and read at startup and refresh, but no configuration sets, including per-environment sets, or configuration-server workload are implemented.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://config/README.md#L59-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a6ba5e7987fe6cf194854af7d8354cbbb917a594bcfe45bac732b0fe23d0a2cb:"
        },
        {
